excerpt: "These results demonstrate that interactions among topography, mean flow, internal waves, and submesoscale instabilities play a fundamental role in BBL dynamics, tracer transport, and energy redistribution in dense overflow regions and the deep ocean. By characterizing the restratification and mixing by internal wave breaking, persistent SI-driven off-shelf export, and dense overflow-modified near-inertial wave trapping and reflection, this work provides a framework for interpreting boundary-driven exchange and mixing."
